# The waystation: a settlement at a crossroads, at the size decisions.md entry 007 asked for.
#
# Radius 24 — 49 hexes and 85 m across, eighteen hundred tiles — so a rifle at 55 m and a sentry
# at 45 m have somewhere to be different from each other. Open ground with a walled compound on
# the main road, a stream crossed by one bridge, a barn, a pair of cottages, a ridge, a
# watchtower and two stands of trees. Nothing here has been fought over yet; it exists to show
# that a map this size is forty statements rather than two thousand lines of C#.

map Waystation

# Kit the built-ins do not have. A hedge you can push through but not see through, and the
# planking of the bridge, which is louder underfoot than the road either side of it.
profile hedge height 1.5 cover light passable opaque destructible
ground boardwalk cost 0 noise 1.4

# ---- ground ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fill disc 0,0 r 24 grass

# The stream runs north-west to south-east, west of the compound; the roads are painted after
# it, so where the main road crosses it there is a bridge.
fill line -20,24 to 4,-24 shallow_water
fill line -24,0 to 24,0 gravel
fill line 10,-24 to 10,14 gravel
fill hex -8,0 boardwalk

fill disc -10,6 r 3 rubble
fill disc 6,-16 r 2 shallow_water

# A ridge, high enough that getting up it is a climb, with one cut path on the road side.
fill disc -12,-6 r 3 h 1.5
stairs -8,-6 -9,-6

# ---- the compound -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Paved inside, a solid wall all round, a gate at each end of the main road, and a drain under
# the south wall that somebody small and patient could crawl through.
fill disc 0,0 r 4 floor
enclose solid disc 0,0 r 4
breach 4,0 ne
breach -4,0 sw
link crawl -1,-3 -1,-4

# Sandbags outside the east gate, covering the road.
wall low hexes 5,-1 5,1 ne

# The house in the middle: a door on the south side, a flat roof with a parapet, and a ladder
# up from the yard on the east.
enclose solid disc 0,1 r 1
breach 0,0 s
fill disc 0,1 r 1 layer 1 h 3
enclose railing disc 0,1 r 1 layer 1
ladder 2,1@0 1,1@1

# ---- outbuildings -------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The barn: head-high walls you could climb, and one door on the west.
fill disc 14,-6 r 2 floor
enclose high disc 14,-6 r 2
breach 12,-6 sw

# Two cottages in the rubble, sharing a wall, door facing the road.
fill hexes -12,8 -12,9 -11,8 floor
enclose solid hexes -12,8 -12,9 -11,8
wall solid hex -12,8 n
breach -11,8 se

# The watchtower: a platform four metres up, railed, ladder only.
fill hex 16,-14 layer 1 h 4
enclose railing hex 16,-14 layer 1
ladder 16,-14@0 16,-14@1

# Ruins by the east road: the odd wall left standing.
chord high 20,-9 0-2
chord low 20,-8 1-3
chord low 21,-10 3-5

# ---- cover in the open --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Two stands of trees, dense enough to hide in and walk through.
wall screen disc 14,6 r 2 all
wall screen disc -6,-14 r 1 all

# Hedgerows along the field boundaries north of the road.
wall hedge line 2,6 to 2,14 nw sw
wall hedge line -14,14 to -6,14 n
